WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.840
Thermal imaging senses infrared radiation emitted and reflected by surfaces and converts

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:06.816
differences into a visible display.

00:00:06.816 --> 00:00:11.161
The image represents apparent temperature patterns, not ordinary color, material identity,

00:00:11.161 --> 00:00:14.717
or a complete explanation of what caused the pattern.

00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:19.457
A visible-light camera records reflected light that human eyes can normally see.

00:00:19.457 --> 00:00:24.198
A thermal sensor works in an infrared range and can reveal contrast

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:26.963
that remains invisible to an ordinary camera,

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:29.728
especially when surfaces have different thermal behavior.

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:33.283
Common uses include drone and ground inspections, facility maintenance,

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:37.234
electrical or mechanical screening, solar arrays, building-envelope review, search support,

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.209
fireground awareness, safety, and security.

00:00:39.209 --> 00:00:43.160
Each use requires different equipment, timing, distance, training, and interpretation.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.690
Thermal imagery can show that one area appears warmer or cooler than its background.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.665
It usually cannot prove why.

00:00:50.665 --> 00:00:54.221
Sun exposure, airflow, moisture, material, reflection, geometry, retained heat,

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:56.986
and sensor settings may create similar patterns.

00:00:56.986 --> 00:01:00.936
Thermal cameras generally observe radiation from surfaces in their view.

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:06.467
They do not provide magical vision through walls, roofs, clothing, smoke, or every obstruction.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:10.417
Apparent patterns may reflect surface effects rather than hidden conditions.

00:01:10.417 --> 00:01:12.788
Safety and lawful purpose come first.

00:01:12.788 --> 00:01:17.133
Collection must follow aviation, site, electrical, fire, privacy, and organizational controls.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:21.479
A thermal sensor does not authorize entry, close approach, intrusive observation,

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:23.849
or work beyond the operator's competence.

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:27.009
Treat thermal imagery as evidence that needs context.

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:31.355
Preserve source files and conditions, compare with expected behavior, seek corroboration,

00:01:31.355 --> 00:01:32.145
state limitations,

00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:35.700
and involve a qualified specialist before making high-consequence conclusions.
